course: dictionary
lesson: 4080
title: Words without words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gesture is a movement of your hand, head or body that shows a meaning. Waving, nodding and pointing are all gestures. Sometimes a gesture says more than words can.
explain: A gesture can also be something you do to show a feeling, especially kindness. «Most arguments end, people say sorry in words or with a kind gesture.» Here, a kind gesture is an action that shows you are sorry, even before you speak.
explain: Gesture can be a verb too. «She gestured to the door» means she moved her hand or head to show where to go. Look for the clue in the sentence: she did not speak, she showed it with her body.
explain: Gestures are body language. «Be patient with a classmate who is still learning English: speak slowly, use gestures and pictures, and each week they will understand more.» When words are hard, a gesture can help someone understand. Remember that some gestures mean different things in different countries, so be careful.
fact: A gesture is a movement of your hand, head or body that shows a meaning.
fact: «A kind gesture» is something you do to show a feeling, especially kindness.
fact: «Gestured» is the past tense of the verb gesture: it means moved your hand or head to show something.
fact: Gestures are body language, and in stories they can show how a character feels without any words.
fact: Some gestures, like a thumbs up, can mean different things in different countries, so think before you use one.
exercise: «She gestured to the door.» What does gestured mean here? | Shut the door quietly | Knocked three times on the door | Opened a window to let in air | *Moved her hand or head to show the way out
exercise: «Most arguments end when people say sorry in words or with a kind gesture.» What is a kind gesture? | A rule that everyone must follow | A loud shout across the room | *An action that shows you are sorry or kind | A long letter of complaint
exercise: «Use gestures and pictures» helps a classmate who is still learning English. Why? | They stop the classmate from speaking | *They show meaning without needing every word | They are only for fun | They make the words longer
test: «He made a friendly gesture by waving at the new girl.» What does friendly gesture mean? | A loud noise in the playground | An angry shout | A long speech about rules | *A kind movement that shows he is welcoming
test: A story says the old man «gestured towards the hills». What did he do? | He wrote a poem about the hills | *He moved his hand to point at the hills | He ran up the hills | He fell asleep on the hills
exam: Why must you be careful when you use a thumbs up gesture with people from other countries? | *Because it can mean different things in different countries | Because it always means the same thing everywhere | Because it is against the rules | Because it makes people laugh
